On expanding of that sidenote of your post:

Slash'Em added "doppelganger-kind", "drovenkind", "hobbit-kind",
"lycanthropehood", "vampirehood" for the new races.

The German versions of NetHack use the suffix "-heit" (which equals
in current use more or less to English"-kind" whereas "-heit" and
"-hood" descended from the same Germanic word [see links below]) for
all races ("Menschheit", "Elbenheit", "Zwergenheit", etc.).

Spanish NetHack also has the suffix "-dad" added to all races
("humanidad", "elfidad", etc.).

The Japanese versions unfortunately didn't translate it. :(

The incomplete French version has "humanite", the rest of the races
seem to be not translated as they are identical to the English
version.


http://www.etymonline.com/index.php?term=kind

http://www.etymonline.com/index.php?term=-hood
